Package: linux-wireless-manager
Version: __VERSION__
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-setuptools, python3-wheel, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, upower, build-essential, libusb-1.0-0-dev, libudev-dev, libhidapi-hidraw0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1 | gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1
Recommends: gir1.2-notify-0.7, solaar
Maintainer: Bryan Calvo <bryan@city.works>
Homepage: https://github.com/xdoncalvox/LinuxMouseStatus
Description: Battery monitor and settings manager for wireless mice/keyboards
 Linux Wireless Manager shows the battery of wireless mice and keyboards
 in the system tray, warns you with a desktop notification before they
 run out, and lets you change device settings: DPI, polling rate, sleep
 timer and button mapping.
 .
 SteelSeries mice are supported through rivalcfg. Other wireless mice and
 keyboards - Logitech receivers, Bluetooth - are read through UPower, with
 Logitech settings available through Solaar when it's installed.
 .
 This package installs a private Python virtualenv under
 /usr/lib/linux-wireless-manager/venv at configure time (network access is
 required then, to fetch rivalcfg from PyPI) rather than depending on
 packaged Python libraries, since rivalcfg isn't packaged for Debian/Ubuntu.
